# Docs Site Formatting

This rule covers the site-specific mechanics of planton.ai/docs — frontmatter schema, link format, icon names, order conventions, and Markdown syntax. It does NOT cover writing strategy, source verification, or quality standards; those live in the planton monorepo's documentation rules and are loaded via `@update-planton-ai-docs`.

## Frontmatter Schema

Every page under `site/public/docs/` requires YAML frontmatter:

```yaml
---
title: "Page Title"
description: "One-line description for SEO and sidebar hover. Max 160 chars."
icon: icon-name
order: 10
tags:
  - Tag1
---
```

**Required**: `title`, `description`, `icon`, `order`
**Optional**: `tags` (string array), `badge` (short label like "Beta", "New", "Deprecated")

## Order Conventions

- Section directories use base order increments: 10, 20, 30, 40, ...
- Section `index.md` inherits the directory's order
- Getting-started pages: order 15
- Content pages within a section: 20, 25, 30, 35, ... (increments of 5 or 10)
- Reference pages: 80-90

Current section order: Platform (10), Connections (20), Infrastructure (30), CI/CD (40), Secrets (45), Variables (47), Operations (50), Runner (60), Security (70), Teams and Access (80), CLI (90).

## Icon Reference

Icons are resolved by `src/app/(root)/docs/utils/fileSystem.ts`. Use the string name in frontmatter; the renderer maps it to an emoji.

Commonly used in docs:

| Name | Emoji | Typical Use |
|------|-------|-------------|
| `platform` | 🏢 | Platform section |
| `concepts` | 🧩 | Core concepts |
| `tour` | 🧭 | Platform tour |
| `hierarchy` | 🌳 | Resource hierarchy |
| `cloud` | ☁️ | Infra components, infrastructure |
| `service` | 🛎️ | Services |
| `pipeline` | 🔗 | Pipelines, integrations |
| `deployment` | 🚀 | Deployment, getting started |
| `security` | 🔒 | Security, encryption |
| `key` | 🔑 | Connections, credentials |
| `billing` | 💰 | Billing |
| `welcome` | 👋 | Welcome, index pages |
| `gear` | ⚙️ | Configuration, settings |
| `code` | 💻 | CLI, code |
| `book` | 📚 | Documentation |
| `guide` | 🗺️ | Guides |
| `users` | 👥 | Teams, community |
| `wrench` | 🔧 | Operations, tools |
| `unlock` | 🔓 | Open source |

Full list: 200+ entries in `fileSystem.ts` `iconMap`. If an icon name is not found, the renderer falls back to pattern matching on the filename.

## Markdown Conventions

- Fenced code blocks with language tags: `bash`, `yaml`, `json`, `ts`, `tsx`, `js`, `go`, `java`, `proto`, `hcl`, `dockerfile`, `sql`, `diff`, `text`, `mermaid`
- Inline code with backticks for commands, file names, identifiers, and config keys
- Internal links: absolute paths from docs root, no `.md` extension — `/docs/infrastructure/infra-components`
- Anchor links: auto-generated from headings — `/docs/cli#install-on-windows`
- No custom anchor syntax `{#custom-id}` — renders literally, does not work
- Callouts: blockquotes with a bold lead — `> **Note:**`, `> **Tip:**`, `> **Warning:**`
- Collapsible sections: `<details><summary>Title</summary>...</details>`

## Sidebar Generation

Driven by `src/app/(root)/docs/utils/fileSystem.ts`:

- Auto-generated from the filesystem under `site/public/docs/`
- Files/directories starting with `_` or `.` are excluded
- `index.md` becomes the directory title page (not shown as separate sidebar entry)
- Sorted by: `order` field, then type (directories first), then alphabetical
- Only `.md` files are processed — other extensions (`.napkin-prompt`, `.asciinema-script`) are invisible

